React is a JavaScript library used to build user interfaces (UI), especially for websites and web applications.

It was created by Facebook (Meta) to make building complex websites easier, faster, and more organized.

Think of React as LEGO blocks.

Instead of building the whole website at once, you build small reusable pieces and connect them.

For example:

Navbar
Login Form
Search Bar
Product Card
Footer

Each of these is called a Component.

Why was React created?

Suppose you're making Instagram.

When someone likes a post:

Without React:

The browser may reload or update a large part of the page.

With React:

Only the Like button and like count change.
Everything else stays the same.

This makes websites much faster.


